<span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Buying vs Renting</span>
<h1>Students: Resale Planning for Hanoi Motorbikes | Hanoi Motorbike Guide</h1>
<p>Every motorbike a student buys in Hanoi comes with a second appointment already written, the day it has to become money again, and the only question is whether that appointment is planned or improvised. Resale is where ownership keeps its most expensive secrets, because the purchase price was negotiated in an afternoon but the exit is negotiated at the worst hour of the semester. This guide plans that exit honestly: no invented market prices, no folklore about which model holds value, and every live requirement handed to the official sources and the neutral desk where it belongs.</p>
<p>The machines, the briefing and the honest numbers come from Motorbike Rental - Nguyen Tu, 112 Nguyen Van Cu in Long Bien, Hanoi, open daily 09:00 to 21:00, where the desk has watched semesters of machines come and go and knows exactly what the next buyer asks first. Begin at the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-for-sale/">motorbike for sale hub</a>, study the long-stay arrangements on the <a href="/monthly-motorbike-rental-hanoi/">monthly motorbike rental</a> page, check the verified figures on the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">Hanoi motorbike rental cost</a> hub, review the <a href="/motorbike-guides/">motorbike guides</a> for maintenance and safety, and keep <a href="/renting-a-motorbike-in-vietnam/">renting a motorbike in Vietnam</a> open for the legal layer.</p>
